WNXT-PROD-USER-ASG (Auto Scaling Group)
Dynamic scaling policy
- policy type : Target Tracking Scaling
- Scaling policy name : WNXT-PROD-USER-ASG-TargetTracking-Sessions
- Metric type : Custom CloudWatch Metric

Custom metric JSON:
{
"CustomizedMetricSpecification": {
"MetricName": "Sessions",
"Namespace": "Ganz/Webkinz",
"Dimensions": [
{
"Name": "AutoScalingGroupName",
"Value": "WNXT-PROD-USER-ASG"
},
{
"Name": "ClusterName",
"Value": "WNXT-PROD-CLUSTER"
}
],
"Statistic": "Average"
}
}


@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@ Since we have only 1 or 2 instances in the ASG, YOYO can happen

To prevent  YOYO,

We will not let Target Tracking scale in automatically:

Target Tracking = scale out only
Step Scaling = controlled scale in

And make scale-in very conservative, for example:

Scale in only if Sessions < 4 per instance for 30 minutes
Remove 1 instance

----------
- check mark the "Disable scale in" option in the Target Tracking policy settings to ensure that the ASG does not scale in automatically based on the target tracking metric.

- Create Step Scaling Policy for Scale In

Configuration Summary
Target Tracking:
  Scale Out → Sessions > 8.0 ✅
  DisableScaleIn = true ✅

Step Scaling Scale In:
  Threshold  = 2.4 (30% of 8.0)
  Duration   = 30 minutes (30 × 60s periods)
  Remove     = 1 instance at a time

